<title>GERMANY: Bertelsmann says cartel office critical of Murdoch.</title>
<headline>Bertelsmann says cartel office critical of Murdoch.</headline>
<dateline>GUETERSLOH, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bertelsmann AG said on Wednesday that German cartel authorities viewed any involvement by Rupert Murdoch in German pay-TV broadcaster Premiere critically.</p>
<p>Clarifying earlier remarks by board member Thomas Middlehoff which were quoted by Reuters, the company issued a statement saying that there was &quot;evidence&quot; that the Berlin cartel office was critical.</p>
<p>But the statement denied a verbatim quote of Middlehof saying that Bertelsmann had received a letter saying the cartel office would block such a move.</p>
<p>British satellite pay-TV broadcaster BSkyB, in which Murdoch's News Corp owns 40 percent, has been promised a 25 percent stake in Premiere as part of Murdoch's alliance with Bavarian media mogul Leo Kirch.</p>
<p>Middelhoff said said BSkyB's involvement with Kirch's DF1 is thus thrown into question.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
